[1;33m[WARN][0m   Review: changes_requested (9 issue(s)) — The implementation attempts to address the prescribed root cause by modifying ContentstackProvider to use useState+useEffect for live preview content and threading previewConfig from getStaticProps. However, it has critical issues: (1) the Contentstack management token is exposed to the client-side browser bundle — a security vulnerability; (2) only 'page' content is updated during live preview, so edits to other content types (header, footer, etc.) won't appear; (3) a new Stack instance is created on every hashchange instead of registering the SDK's onContentUpdate callback once as prescribed; (4) zero vitest unit tests were added. The approach of using hashchange events instead of the SDK's live preview callback is a deviation from the prescribed minimal fix and may not reliably capture all preview update events. The implementation needs significant rework before it can meet all acceptance criteria.

