[1;33m[WARN][0m   Review: changes_requested (8 issue(s)) — The implementation partially addresses the prescribed root cause — ContentstackContext.tsx has been changed from a static useMemo to useState+useEffect with live preview fetching, and getStaticProps detects context.preview and computes previewConfig. However, multiple blockers prevent the feature from working end-to-end: (1) previewConfig is computed in getStaticProps but never passed from the Page component to ContentstackProvider, so preview mode never activates; (2) only 'page' content is updated during live preview, not header/footer/serviceAlerts/etc.; (3) a new Stack instance is created on every fetch instead of reusing a client; (4) real-time updates rely on hashchange events rather than the SDK's livePreview callback; (5) zero unit tests exist for the new functionality. The verdict is changes_requested.

